alchemical master of Ebon Shadow that accidentally crossed into the Labyrinth and was partly corrupted) and Fair Folk (because exploring dreams can lead into very strange places on occasion and this time the Viator found &quot;friends&quot;, or at least pliant minions). Fun times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-10-2021, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T17:36:30-07:00","id":1443428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1443421#post1443421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Viator of Nullspace, if memory tricks me not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! Silly me. Though I do like the acidentental Spawn image my mistake invokes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1443421#post1443421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Truth be told, i' once made a Shadow Warriors/Transformer-esque game involving war in Autochtonia among metal elementals and mortal communities associated with them. Also some crossing over with Abyssals (the weird prison cube in the Labyrinth actually being a Ess6 alchemical master of Ebon Shadow that accidentally crossed into the Labyrinth and was partly corrupted) and Fair Folk (because exploring dreams can lead into very strange places on occasion and this time the Viator found &quot;friends&quot;, or at least pliant minions). Fun times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that sounds like an awesome game. How did it do with the Viator/Fae conflict?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T01:54:18-07:00","id":1443452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1443359#post1443359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I fully accept this. Yes. This is excellent.</div> </div> </div> </div>The follow-up is:<br /> <br /> Very few Americans speak Russian. But just about all Americans recognise the name &quot;Kalashnikov&quot; or &quot;AK-47&quot;.<br /> <br /> Likewise, whilst each language in Creation has its own words for &quot;magic sword&quot; and &quot;ridiculously large hammer&quot;, the Old Realm &quot;daiklave&quot; is understood <i>basically univerally</i> across Creation.<br /> <br /> &quot;The tribe clearly doesn't speak Foresttongue. They chatter back and forth in their own language, deciding what to do you with you. The only word you can understand is when the priestess says 'daiklave'.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T06:44:17-07:00","id":1443469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1443452#post1443452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The follow-up is:<br /> <br /> Very few Americans speak Russian. But just about all Americans recognise the name &quot;Kalashnikov&quot; or &quot;AK-47&quot;.<br /> <br /> Likewise, whilst each language in Creation has its own words for &quot;magic sword&quot; and &quot;ridiculously large hammer&quot;, the Old Realm &quot;daiklave&quot; is understood <i>basically univerally</i> across Creation.<br /> <br /> &quot;The tribe clearly doesn't speak Foresttongue. They chatter back and forth in their own language, deciding what to do you with you. The only word you can understand is when the priestess says 'daiklave'.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In that same vein, after some conversations with one of my players I've come to the understanding that the word 'Artifact' doesn't make much sense as an in-setting thing, and neither does the idea of a unified system of Artifact <i>crafting</i>. Like, a crafter who hails from a Shogunate-Era tradition of forging blue jade on a special mountaintop cloud-anvil maintained through ancient rituals and the appeasement of spirits of the sky would look at you with naked confusion if you brought them a chunk of Orichalcum and asked them to make you a sword with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T16:53:36-07:00","id":1444091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1443089#post1443089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I base this on how the description of the canon ending in <i>Ascension</i> resembles the Deep Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s funny because I have an opposite headcanon to this: Consensus reality is what would happen to Creation without the Loom of Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T11:25:22-07:00","id":1444361,"title":"","content":"The white veil society was started as an effort by a Lunar to weaken the realm by having dynasts assassinate one another, it has long since spiraled out control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T21:31:48-07:00","id":1444440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1444361#post1444361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The white veil society was started as an effort by a Lunar to weaken the realm by having dynasts assassinate one another, it has long since spiraled out control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Or would be if the books weren't clear that there is no White Veil Society \ud83d\ude08","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T13:27:00-07:00","id":1444706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1444361#post1444361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The white veil society was started as an effort by a Lunar to weaken the realm by having dynasts assassinate one another, it has long since spiraled out control.</div> </div> </div> </div>My headcanon is much the same, only the Scarlet Empress started it as a way to weaken the Realm by having Dynasts assassinate each other (so that they'd always be dependent on her being at the top, and that any uppity newcomer can die screaming).<br /> <br /> The current state of affairs is a bit like Fight Club.<br /> <br /> &quot;Didn't you start that one?&quot;<br /> &quot;No, I thought you did!&quot;<br /> <br /> It's thoroughly out of control and may well be why she's missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T09:36:27-07:00","id":1446452,"title":"","content":"If you look hard enough in the Deep Underground, you will find Fraggles eating the works of the Mountain Folk, which are the same as the Doozers, and yes, their relative sizes to each other are the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T06:54:37-07:00","id":1446595,"title":"","content":"The Tarpan wastes do not exist as a result of failing solar magic.<br /> <br /> It is true that solar magic was what made the Tarpan Wastes pleasant and fertile once long ago. But the chosen of elements, especially wood, should not be incapable of ecological restoration and manipulation. They are more manual about it than their celestial counterparts. But the Dragon-bloods are in no way incompetent in the ways of magic.<br /> <br /> It's also true that the solar magic failed. But dragon-blood built their own solutions to keep the fields going. However, a lunar circle of the silver pact had managed to copy a dragonline schematic of the Tarpan jungle and practiced a few spells and theorized a way to change the aspect of the manses and destroying a large part of the blessed isle.<br /> <br /> They snuck in and put their plan into action but were detected when the elemental energies started behaving strangely and the dynasts came to stop them. The Lunars were desperate and instead of taking the chance to flee they chose to finish the ritual early. The manse detonated, as well as several more as a result of the cascading dragon-lines. Almost every manse within the wastes changed element and the energies are still very messed up to this day.<br /> <br /> But the work to restore the wastes were going along well during the empress reign. An Imperial sponsored restoration project kept House Mnemon, Nellens and Ledaal busy to work on making the area pleasantly liveable once again. This project was among the first to be abandoned when the empress disappeared. But during the two decades since the Tarpan catastrophe House of bells has had the area as a testing ground for last year students against the mutants, crazy elementals and few remaining beastfolk that survived the destruction. <br /> <br /> This is part of a setting headcanon project to make solars less present in the setting several millennia after their disappearence. Make the other celestial more present, but most importantly, not have the Dragon-blooded as incompetent or sadistic. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13615-slovorg","name":"slovorg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T07:13:15-07:00","id":1446597,"title":"","content":"<b>*points upwards*</b><br /> <br /> I like that one. Generally speaking I change a bit on how the setting views the DBs and the Celestials. Remember. DBs are exalted too. Solar-effecting magic is truly few and far between, with a whole lot of jury-rigging, repurposing, and frankly speaking paving over of the previous era's achievements and monuments. And also, DBs have a lot of boosts to making smaller, weaker artifacts. They just... spam them. (Yeah, I know this contradicts 3e).<br /> <br /> Edit: And by that, I mean that they certainly can't make powerful evocations, but if you're a DB-level stuff, you can get a pack of assistants and crank out Artifact 2s or 3s at a respectable rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 04-30-2021, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T07:27:50-07:00","id":1446599,"title":"","content":"Exactly. I'm also annoyed at how reading certain books it seems like every solar was a Solar circle crafting twilight and every cool thing was made by them. It lessens everyone. Especially Dragon-blooded. I've yet to get to the lunar dominions yet in my writetrough, but there's (presumably) some incredible things done with lunar workings, millennia of animal husbandry and places in mirror realms and shadow terretories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13615-slovorg","name":"slovorg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T10:26:31-07:00","id":1446629,"title":"","content":"Alright, I'll write mine.<br /> <br /> There is a way to infuse magical powers inside people in otherwise non-magical people. Normally, that's something that can only be accomplished by an Exaltation or, in a very limited way, by having a spirit of some kind bless you (side note, it's also my headcanon that there are a lot of X-blooded that are not really X-blooded as X-blessed, particularly the weaker ones). However, you can do something like that by working with Elemental Essence, which is far easier than using any other type of Essence since Elemental Essence is by far the more 'attuned' to mortals (you can do it with other types of Essence but you have to be a sorcerer or a Celestial Exalt to do something like that). It's still a laborious process that requires harmonization between the would-be empowered receiver and an Elemental. The results are likely minor unless you're particularly skilled, lucky, or working with a very powerful Elemental, but you can end up with something that vaguely resembles an element-themed God-blood. <br /> <br /> The problem is that you require a powerful (Essence 4 or 5) Dragon-blooded as a mediator between the two different Essences, and an Elemental willing to help (coercion works but it's inadvisable). Both are actually quite rare since Dragonblooded would not like to have people with powers similar to theirs around and Elementals don't actually gain anything from this exchange and it's very taxing for them.<br /> <br /> It's also possible to use this 'ritual' on non-Dragonblooded Exalted, which give them some minor elemental power (in the form of Spirit Charms), but the requirements are even more strict, like having both the Dragon-blooded and the Elemental have Essence higher than the Exalted in question.<br /> <br /> An even more rare variant of the rituals can, theoretically, be used to empower a Dragonblooded, with very different results compared to the mortal or Exalted one. The effects are more relative to making their Essence equally attuned to every element, with every harmonization reducing the cost of their Charms and getting them extra power to their Excellencies... but the problem with this particular procedure is that it requires a Dragon-blooded to have reached the absolute peak of spiritual enlightenment and the Elemental be even more powerful (so Essence 5 and 6 respectively). Needless to say, the conditions make it very unlikely a Dragonblood is ever going to be able to even attempt this ritual, never mind doing it four times to achieve perfect harmonization with all elements... but if one was able to, the reward would be worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T19:14:52-07:00","id":1446716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>slovorg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1446599#post1446599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. I'm also annoyed at how reading certain books it seems like every solar was a Solar circle crafting twilight and every cool thing was made by them. It lessens everyone. Especially Dragon-blooded. I've yet to get to the lunar dominions yet in my writetrough, but there's (presumably) some incredible things done with lunar workings, millennia of animal husbandry and places in mirror realms and shadow terretories.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Actually you know what? I have a problem with... the entire thing in general. I think I've seen too much Mage the Ascension but for some reason I'm irked that there's this focus on Twilights. Let's expand this shit. Mage generally just had 'five' powers, and was much more detached from common sense and reality than Exalted, which is a feat in and of itself. Adding to that their powerset is a whole lot more flexible than Exalted and capable of doing so much more... I think not everyone needs to do make an equivalent, but I still think that there's space for setting-warping and changing things that *don't* need to make sorcery or artifice. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Eternal Army: An army of dour, grey soldiery, meant to protect a local Solar's dominions from the many depradations of the Fae and the Lunar that lead them. The mutual kill lead to the dissolving of the Dead's army and the protection of the lands... for now. But the Wyld stayed, and the Fae still had those who were more intelligent than most, and so, the war continued on. The Eternal Army is an army specially trained by the Solar in anti-fae tactics, specializing in murdering supernatural opponents and living in harsh conditions. Those who join the Eternal Army find that they learn the anti-Fae martial arts easier, and that they are as comfortable in a swamp as they are in a bedroom. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">One Day, a Hero Shall Rise: A set of stories and social conventions and cultural mores a storyteller, permanently affecting a set of cultures. The stories call for a specific set of qualities, whether in ordinary humans or gods or kings. And when those qualities are broken and widespread damage is done, whether a king who worships a demon or a god that is selling his people to the Fae, a Hero rises up to defeat him. The Hero has bonuses, increased stats, and custom merits to help him defeat the foe he faces. And he is also the exemplar of the qualities required of the stories. There is nothing obvious about this, seemingly to the naked eye a natural cycle and cultural consequence. Only the Sidereals and those with Essence Sight even have a hope of figuring out what is happening. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Glory to the State: First there was Man. And then, Man created the State. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A specially created government bureaucracy ruling a kingdom in the Far Reaches. A set of rituals, customs, prayers, and specially designed buildings and organizations according to geomantic and arcane principles. The bureaucracy has several bonuses, especially when fighting off enemies and helping the people under the control of the State, as long as they work according to the First Founder's Principles. And when they do not, their power slackens, weakens, and they are overthrown. Only for their predecessors to slowly be molded by chance and cultural drift to resemble their predecessors, but without the corruption. <br /> <br /> So on and so forth. Ordinary martial artists can start schools. Exalted Martial artists can, with sufficient effort, create martial arts schools with special powers or blessings. Ordinary men can write books. Exalted writers can make stories that shake the world, and can have effects beyond the written word. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T02:13:34-07:00","id":1446760,"title":"","content":"For me, I'm pretty sure the reason is that when the books portray cool effects that remain for several ages only the crafting and sorcerous workings remain. All the work of dawn castes, zeniths and eclipses are forgotten. The nights are kind of forgotten by design. That limits character concepts gained from reading. <br /> Why would you want to play the greatest and kindest king when it's portrayed time and time again that the nation will crumble the second you die of age? Why would you want to play a general when usurpation teaches that solars were beaten by their own troops? And so on. But the casters, their buildings, artefacts, spells and legacies remain. Sometimes reading the realm it seems as if a twilight long dead(I doubt all twilights were solar circle crafters) has more of a say in how the Blessed isle is shaped than some entire Great Houses. This is part of the reason for the setting rewrite to make all exalted matter. Each idea on it's own is great, but there's too much of it.<br /> <br /> But I really like your ideas Accelerator. Well thought out. Might use them as inspiration in my setting. Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> And to keep things on topic:<br /> <br /> The Imperial road started falling into disrepair during the shogunate and during the Great Contagion and the Balorian invasion the last few bits of the magic was destroyed by 3 sidereals (1 battle, 1 endings and 1 journey) that were alive to delay the invading armies. They had spotted a thin hope that the fey armies could be stopped, but more time was needed. Without this action it was unclear if the Empress could have breached the imperial manse in time.<br /> <br /> Later during the Empress reign history records of the old Imperial road surfaced and the help it could have posed to the invaders. An edict was put forward to the masons of the Blessed Isle to make a road that outdid the Imperial road. Mnemon did so after discussing some startlingly difficult crafting techniques with a yellow-eyed assistant. House Nellens, Cynis, Ragara and Iselsi negotiated with Mnemon to release the schematic to the Heptagram so the knowledge would not die if House Menmon did. Each Prefecture is mandated to maintain their roads with prayers, sacrifices of granite and bellflowers and a respectful military presence. Variations of granite and local bellflowers makes each prefecture imperial road slightly different. The road in Lord's Crossings Dominion is nicknamed the Blue Steps and the similar name in Eagle Prefecture is Water's Run. The first one since it gains a slightly blue sheen, and Eagle Prefecture as it has become a tradition to pick the flowers in the early season of water as a marathon contest, giving the name to both the contest and the road.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13615-slovorg","name":"slovorg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T23:50:46-07:00","id":1447776,"title":"","content":"There is a certain platonic ideal within Exalted. An Exalted with a bow and arrow is just as good with a plasma cannon or a flintlock rifle or whatever..... <br /> <br /> Same thing for tools. A smith-god with a hammer and forge can easily transform them into a 3D printer, CNC machine, a lathe... but it doesn't matter, it just needs a concept of a 'creation tool'. Same thing for a war god. Spears can work. So can flintlock rifles, or machine guns, or gatling guns, or a telescoping sword composed out of shapeshifting metal alloys and a disintegration field. <br /> <br /> The weapons of the gods change with the times, and also dependent on who precisely is looking at them, and their own view of the world. The symbols change, but the meaning is the same. 'That which brings death to others' or 'this person is wealthy' or 'the wearer is knowledgeable'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T22:19:20-07:00","id":1449091,"title":"","content":"Beast-blooded are descended from a Lunar that held their beast's totem. This is not to say that all Lunar children are clearly beast-blooded, or that it's impossible for beastmen to arise in another fashion, but that it is the most common method of their creation.<br /> <br /> Occasionally, a beast-blooded will be born to otherwise human parents. This is usually because a Lunar of that totem (or another beast-blood) is present somewhere in the humans' ancestral line. In that way, it is similar to the Dragon's blood, something that Lunars are fully aware of and are incredibly uncomfortable with. In fact, Such beastblooded are looked at somewhat askance, as if their existence cheapens the &quot;true&quot; beast-blooded. The irony of treating these 'men-born' the same manner that the Realm treats Outcastes is lost on most Lunars.<br /> <br /> There are rumors that Lunars must engage in bestiality to produce beast-blooded for obvious reasons, but this is Immaculate propaganda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T20:13:00-07:00","id":1451605,"title":"","content":"There's a certain type of fish in the western oceans, near heavily aspected earth demenses. The fish are shiny, silvery scales, and a large fat body. Some eat it, deciding that they look delicious. Those who are more clever don't. The fish have a powerful tendency to absorb from their surroundings... including heavy metals. Yes, that includes mercury. Any fish in the sea contains a higher amount of heavy metals than any other fish, and this is especially true for demense heavy areas. <br /> <br /> The fish are from a shogunate breeding project which attempts to harvest micro-sized precious magical materials and gold from the ocean, using the fish as methods to concentate them. However, genetic drift has caused the mechanism to take in all metals, not just a select few. A specialized breeding program can narrow it down again, letting men harvest fish for gold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T09:29:04-07:00","id":1452491,"title":"","content":"Kind of based on stuff from the recent novella <b>The Silence of Our Ancestors</b>, some things on stars came ot mind.<br /> <br /> Mostly I kind of imagine that while most htings move East-to-West, and mostly on the ecliptic, they don't do so as a fixed dome like we usually see on Earth. INstead there's &quot;layers&quot; to them, with the different constellations being relatively fixed as they move over the night, but they move at different speeds in relation to one-another without crossing. They all take 24 hours to go around, but do so at slightly off form one-another, and there's a bit of delay here and htere that allows them to at times be in relaion to eacohter. The planets kind of do this too, and so it creates this 30-bodied mess that helps inform how astrology works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T14:06:37-07:00","id":1452821,"title":"","content":"I'm almost certain that back in the day, Savage Seas established that Creation's sky was a lot more chaotic than that of Earth, presumably to give some credence to the idea of using them to divine anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T18:15:27-07:00","id":1452839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1452821#post1452821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm almost certain that back in the day, Savage Seas established that Creation's sky was a lot more chaotic than that of Earth, presumably to give some credence to the idea of using them to divine anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>The basic image I like to use is an orrery like you can see on Chejob Kejak's desk in his chapter ficiton in the orignal 1e corebook. To me rather than the just the planets, one probably could make one with more bands that represen thte constellations and plaents and sun and moon. And you'd probably have a disk in the middle instead of a sphere like we see usually on Earth ones. It's a neat image to me that I think helps explain how I'm see this I guess &lt;_&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T02:40:16-07:00","id":1452876,"title":"","content":"While I don't know if or how they plan to integrate the four &quot;Getimian asteroids&quot; as entities, in the case that they won't be presented as such (that is, being referenced only through the Caste Marks), that's how I'll play it-<br /> <br /> When the Getimians were created, Sacheverell and Oramus divided the price of Exaltation between them, and leaving their mark over their Essence. Sacheverell, being passive and unmoving, embodies the Still Essence, creating the &quot;cold seasons Castes&quot;. Oramus, being active and expanding, embodies the Flowing Essence, creating the &quot;hot seasons Castes&quot;. However, the process of Exaltation also melded their Essence together, creating a balance between opposites, and giving a rise to strange entities within them. The Flowing within the Still which is the mark of Oramus upon Sacheverell is Ceres of the Autumn Caste. The Still within the Still which is Sacheverell at his purest is Vesta of the Winter Caste. The Still within the Flowing which is the mark of Sacheverell upon Oramus is Juno of the Spring Caste. Finally, The Flowing within the Flowing which is Oramus at his purest is Pallas of the Summer Caste. Those changes within their Essence, as well as the form that their Exaltation have taken, was what terrified those ancient and caused them to seal the Getimian Exaltation, attempting to silence the strange voices which they never intended to create.<br /> <br /> (I'm not sure if those were revaled to be the canon associations between asteroids and seasons, but if not just change them accordingly)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T03:58:47-07:00","id":1457564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1446452#post1446452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look hard enough in the Deep Underground, you will find Fraggles eating the works of the Mountain Folk, which are the same as the Doozers, and yes, their relative sizes to each other are the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside, wouldn't that mean Fraggles are about 11-22 feet tall? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Respectable size that can make interactions with them problematic indeed. <br /> <br /> <br /> Do they also seek wisdom from an all-knowing sentient heap of half-eaten jadeborn works &amp; discarded dreams, guarded by rat-like companion spirits? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-24-2021, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T05:26:54-07:00","id":1457567,"title":"","content":"Based on the last episode of Fraggle Rock the magic of the underground adjusts for differences in distances between the Underground and Outer Space, at least for the specific entrances and exits the Fraggles use. Presumably if it can adjust the difference between one state and another it can adjust the difference between head and foot. If that is important.<br /> <br /> That being said, the idea that Marjory is the size of a small city is amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T06:51:27-07:00","id":1457573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1457567#post1457567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on the last episode of Fraggle Rock the magic of the underground adjusts for differences in distances between the Underground and Outer Space, at least for the specific entrances and exits the Fraggles use. Presumably if it can adjust the difference between one state and another it can adjust the difference between head and foot. If that is important.<br /> <br /> That being said, the idea that Marjory is the size of a small city is amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, indeed. And then there's the whole issue of what kind of being would Marjory be in the first place. I can see arguments for her as a terrestrial spirit (goddess of <b>that</b> particular trash heap x a goddess of trash heaps as a whole) or elemental (she <b>is </b>the trash heap x something that inhabits/oversees it) both, with some signs of <b><i>sidereal </i></b>ressonance at that (how she &quot;knows everything&quot; through other beings' discarded possessions hints at Secrets and Endings both, if one stops to think about it).<br /> <br /> Hmmm, if memory tricks me not, there's a scene into 3e's intro story that introduces the possibility of elementals of wood being generated from the patterns of human/urban behaviour in population centers like Wu-Jian....<br /> <br /> <b>This </b>one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EX3, pg.09</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">She passed a knot where the clotheslines-web between eight buildings had given rise to a little spirit \u2014 an elemental of wood, a laundry-spider \u2014 and she ducked its fangs, curled through its web, and plummeted towards a gallery four floors below.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmm, looks like Majorly as some pretty peculiar elemental resulting from weird essence confluences happening where all too many dregs - physical, figurative and symbolic - of a society gather, pile up and acquire a life &amp; wisdom all its own could be a thing. A goddess and oracle of the poor, hungry and those who would live from the discarded leftovers of the more affluent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-24-2021, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T19:41:18-07:00","id":1457943,"title":"","content":"One of the more common things created in Exalted's first age was decanters of endless water, and bags of unending grain/ potatoes. This is because the Exalted were, after all, humans. And one of the first human concerns was food. Also, they were in a war, which meant that agricultural areas were the first thing under attack. What was needed was food that did not require infrastructure and can be taken on the march. The passage of years have caused many to be lost. The Realm has a few. Lookshy has many. And a few in the hundred kingdoms have them, warping and transforming the local geopolitics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T21:15:52-07:00","id":1458013,"title":"","content":"Creation isn't that hard to change for PC's. Big epic changes happen about every 12-20 sessions or so. Why? It's <b>Exalted.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T23:49:38-07:00","id":1458026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1458013#post1458013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creation isn't that hard to change for PC's. Big epic changes happen about every 12-20 sessions or so. Why? It's <b>Exalted.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Also, despite the Exalted being Great Men.... they are also not-great men.<br /> <br /> In the sense that despite they have the power and might to shape and warp societies far beyond any ordinary mortal, they are still very much shaped and transformed by the people within that society. A Dragonblooded may have high minded egalitarian beliefs, but most dragonblooded would have those thoughts influenced by the immaculate faith and immaculate order. The Bull of the North may be might beyond belief, but he too was influenced by his society, and that influence drove him to raiding and warfare. Exalts may of course, have great power to reshape society... but their powers simply make it easier to carry out what was being done earlier, but better. And all too often in a way that leaves mortals behind.<br /> <br /> It is only the strange or the older that have the inspiration and separation from their community to think beyond it.<br /> <br /> Which is why there is no industrial revolution in Creation. Exalted tend to simply reshape entire new methods of creating Artifacts for personal use, and new skills and techniques for craftsmen. Better trained troops, unbreakable morale, and battle tactics that can make Admiral Yi weep, insetad of gunpowder cannons and rockets. Usage of the Magical materials and divine blessings to create a chariot that can fly through the air or move a thousand times faster than a horse, rather than an internal combustion engine. Swords that can cut through battalions, but only for essence users.<br /> <br /> edit: There is also the distinct lack of populism. Because, of course the mortals are second stage hands to everything compared to the Exalted. Why bother labouring to create weapons which every single mortal can use, when you can focus your efforts on making the next Stormcaller or Eye of the Fire Dragon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T01:21:20-07:00","id":1458034,"title":"","content":"Since in the corebook's text the landmass of the city-island of Palanquin is described as &quot;four colossal <i>inhuman </i>statues, their features long since weathered away&quot;, instead of the greek soldier seeming dudes of the picture of page 94, i have it being held by Godzilla, Gamera, Gigan &amp; King Ghidorah (&quot;look ma, no hands!&quot;) instead. If they are only statues or the real thing in fossilized/petrified state - well, let's leave that for when i make some game there, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T17:45:35-07:00","id":1458093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1458026#post1458026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bull of the North may be might beyond belief, but he too was influenced by his society, and that influence drove him to raiding and warfare. Exalts may of course, have great power to reshape society... but their powers simply make it easier to carry out what was being done earlier, but better. And all too often in a way that leaves mortals behind.<br /> <br /> It is only the strange or the older that have the inspiration and separation from their community to think beyond it.<br /> <br /> Which is why there is no industrial revolution in Creation. Exalted tend to simply reshape entire new methods of creating Artifacts for personal use, and new skills and techniques for craftsmen. Better trained troops, unbreakable morale, and battle tactics that can make Admiral Yi weep, insetad of gunpowder cannons and rockets. Usage of the Magical materials and divine blessings to create a chariot that can fly through the air or move a thousand times faster than a horse, rather than an internal combustion engine. Swords that can cut through battalions, but only for essence users.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding onto this, the power and plans of the Exalted are such that they don't plan to die. But they invariably do. And since no power is given to the mortals in the first place, they are lost. Wu Chufeng's weather control device is a marvel, but requires essence attunement, a difficulty 4 roll to control, and no one can replicate it. And since there are at best a million dragonblooded and 700 celestial exalted, the exponential growth created by industrial technology is nearly impossible. And since all resources are being spent on unmatchable, singular artifacts...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T15:49:34-07:00","id":1458187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1458034#post1458034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since in the corebook's text the landmass of the city-island of Palanquin is described as &quot;four colossal <i>inhuman </i>statues, their features long since weathered away&quot;, instead of the greek soldier seeming dudes of the picture of page 94, i have it being held by Godzilla, Gamera, Gigan &amp; King Ghidorah (&quot;look ma, no hands!&quot;) instead. If they are only statues or the real thing in fossilized/petrified state - well, let's leave that for when i make some game there, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of not quite exactly those, but I tend to imagine them looking like the statues in teh sanctuary of <b>Shadows of the Colossus</b> more than the humanodis they are in the coreobok illustrationl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T02:43:02-07:00","id":1458797,"title":"","content":"There's a shitload more difference in ages between Exalted. Some got their exaltations when they were children. Child prodigies, those who were born lucky, or kids in situations they really shouldn't be in. Some got them when they were old. Old, accomplished heroes, wrinkled old men filled with regret and shame, or elderly who closed their eyes for what they believed to be their final time, and opened up to find the walls bleeding blood. <br /> <br /> Which yes, that also screws up some dynamics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T07:52:27-07:00","id":1459009,"title":"","content":"Many kinds of folklore and uncanny occult traditions exist across all corners around spiders, specially a variety of species notable for possessing colored dot arrangements resembling the 25 constellations of the skies associated with the five maidens of Fate.<br /> <br /> Their varieties and names are many, but most savants and mystics will sagely nod to the common titles of Constellation Weavers, Pattern Spiders or Star Spiders, with those of dark blue or black bodies and dots in the color of their maiden (yellow for journeys, red for battle and so on) being the most valued by sages, priests, sorcerers and the idle rich with a need for exotic pets.<br /> <br /> Priests of the principalities of Flamula will raise Crimson Banner Spiders in the ceilings of their observatories and when the stars are right for times of battle, have the most auspicious among their champions and generals bitten by them, to further inflame their warrior spirits.<br /> <br /> Folk witches, charlatan and true both, speak of the uses of love philters woven from the silk of Azure Lovers Weavers as protection against either abusive suitors, or the magics of the Fair Folk when dyed in certain tinctures of irondust, while others will stealthily offers love potions capable of inflaming the most improbable passions, supposedly using their ichor, poison, ground flesh or mistures of either, depending on place, maker or supposed power of a specific spider breed.<br /> <br /> In the past the auspicene people were known for the fortune they would draw from the seas through the blessings gathered in delicate but resilient sails woven from the webs of spiders of the Citrine Sanctuary of Journeys, until the secrets of their domestication and weaving techniques were lost with the death of the old generation of priests from before the conquest by the Azure lords of the Coral Archipelago, making the sails that still exist ever more valued relics.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile other speak amid hushed tones of rumors about dead priests that watch over their descendants still, through the many eyes and legs of their cherished wards and have gleaned sorcerous lore from secret places between the stars where they dance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-28-2024, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T16:52:54-07:00","id":1460389,"title":"","content":"Luna is a being comprised of all possible gods and goddesses of the moon, all of the moons she defeated and devoured when Oramus first created her.<br /> <br /> To be clear, I do not mean that Luna took in all of the powers and abilities of the othermoons; I mean they are an actual part of her. Luna is multiple beings, all of whom are both Luna and not one another (in a way like the Trinity in Christian theology). They are all somewhat independent beings and personalities, both part of Luna and separate from her. Now, the &quot;true&quot; Luna - the glue that holds all of these disparate forms and personalities together - was the one who won the right to be the moon goddess and devoured the othermoons. By doing so, she can take the forms of any of her other selves whenever she wishes.<br /> <br /> You may be scratching your head and asking what the point of that is. Luna as the shapeshifting trickster diety is more than capable of just *changing her own form*, is she not? If she wants to be, say, the heavily pregnant man moon, she can just *make herself* that heavily pregnant man. Right?<br /> <br /> Yes. And no.<br /> <br /> See, when a Lunar changes shape, the core essence of what they are is not what's changed. A Lunar that becomes a raccoon is still a Lunar. If a barbarian 'might-makes-right' Lunar eats the heart of a pacifistic noblemen from the Isle, she might be able to imitate him right down to his mannerisms, but ultimately she has not actually *become* him, she just *looks* like him. This is why the Tell exists; no matter how radically your average Lunar alters themselves, they remain who they are at their core. What that actually means is going to vary from Lunar to Lunar; gender, mannerisms, attitude, core beliefs...<br /> <br /> Luna can do this. But she is also capable of changing that core. Sure, she <i>could</i> just wear the skin of what she wants, but that doesn't give the sheer <i>zeal</i> that truly being that person does. Today, she needs to be a trickster; tomorrow, a wise mentor by the road. To one Lunar, she needs to be a mother; to another, a rival that looks uncannily like the Lunar's little brother. To yet another, a shoulder to cry on, or a body to warm the bed. (And once, a particularly snarky food critic. That was a weird day)<br /> <br /> And this is her true strength. She is not one consistent being, not even truly a singular Incarnae in the way that Sol or the Maidens are. She is whatever Creation needs her to be. Gaia's lover, Sol's best friend (with benefits~), a mass murdering monster, an aging sage, a noble hero... She can be any of these things, and all of them.<br /> <br /> Because the Othermoon that sought only for Creation to be safe was the one that defeated her other selves. No other desire was enough - to win no matter the cost, to think and outwit her enemies, not even love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T03:21:02-07:00","id":1463677,"title":"","content":"So, specifically a 2E headcanon, since I doubt the concept of 'children of the earth' will be returning in 3E, but I headcanoned that the term 'children of the earth' originated from an old realm term that was used in the first age in spaces where mortals were theoretically welcome but in practice largely unwelcome as a plausibly-deniable way to denigrate mortals who failed to meet unfair standards. &quot;Some mortals are OK, but, you know, so many of them are just so... children of the earth, if you know what I mean?&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T15:47:28-08:00","id":1469673,"title":"","content":"Lunar spirit shapes for animals with very apparent sexual dimorphism are not specifically confined to the gender of the Exalt's human shape. You can have a woman Lunar with a peafowl spirit shape, and it could have the colourful plumage and distinctive tail feathers; sometimes that means the animal form is male, sometimes it's a uniquely female shape with blue and green feathers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T18:50:02-07:00","id":1491849,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the necro-post, but things have been pretty silent here recently anyway.<br /> <br /> I'm not suggesting that this is in ANY way canon, but I find the concept interesting, so I'm including it in &quot;my&quot; version of the setting.<br /> <br /> Desus, the terrifying abuser from 2nd edition still <i>existed, </i>but not as a Solar. Rather, he was one of the last of the Aurorals, and one of the first generation of Hearteaters.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T12:00:47-08:00","id":1503336,"title":"","content":"Y'danna is a very alien place to its neighbours due to a dualistic pantheon of gods that are believed to occasionally invert between order and chaos which they track through various omens.<br /> This can make the island nation very unpredictable which seems to have aided more than it's hindered it against the rival kingdoms of the Dreaming Sea. This perhaps suggests it's more than just a collection of superstitions, but it may well be that this system of omens was created to allow Y'danna's priesthood to sheppard the fate of the nation by manufacturing or reinterpret the necessary omens to nudge its royal family in a direction they prefer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T14:19:37-08:00","id":1503398,"title":"","content":"Once came to be, sometime between the Divine Revolution and the Niobraran War, the <b>empire of Ur-Anu</b>, a coalition of air elementals aligned with but independent from the Deliberative, a nation so extensive in reach their citizens would come to be known as People of the Air.<br /> <br /> Though solar propaganda would exagerate the relevance of their diplomatic role in supporting the establishment of their nation - to the point of sages of later eras misinterpretating the inhabitants of the aerial citadels and palaces as the &quot;creations of the exalted&quot; in the tales lionizing the exalted or villanizing the anathema - the nation and its many people had a long history and culture very much its own, influenced to some degree by the &quot;adoption&quot; of young sorcerously-created air elementals just released from service in as probationary citizens but barely beyond a superficial (and conveniently self-serving) level.<br /> \u200b<br /> The conflicts of the Usurpation, the Shogunate that followed it, along with the tensions of the Rain Wars between Air and Water courts would lead to the incremental weakening of their civilization that would eventually shatter with the Contagion and Fae Invasion, with the hedonistic palaces of the Cloud People, the belligerent fraternities of nomadic thunderbirds and mysterious empty citadels floating amidst the stormy skies or the highest fog-shrouded mountains as some of the most long-lasting remnants of this long storied legacy.<br /> <br /> One that might be far from completely gone, as the elemental cloudfolk of the windborne City of Blue Gauze, who visit Palanquin to trade with mortals, remember and cherish that memory, spreading the tale (and diaphanous seed) among locals who will share in nostalgia and passion of festivals with them. And some whisper or seek out in secret half-forgotten heirlooms and treasure hidden in plain sight, ancient rumours of a heaven beyond heaven enclosed by elder gods or titans even, in obscure chronicles undone through the turmoil of ages in all but the ever changing retellings on countless voices across the aeons, not the least among them.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-21-2023, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T16:44:45-08:00","id":1503501,"title":"","content":"The decadence and final fall of the People of the Air's civilization was influenced in no small part by a wave of societies and cults formed of masses of mortals offering themselves in virtual slavery &amp; debasement for the sake of escaping the Contagion-plagued metropolises and small kingdoms of the surface world, many of these servants, lovers &amp; playthings to the point of using one magical feather too far and encountering dissolution as clouds &amp; rainfall for that decision.<br /> <br /> In fact all too many thousands EMBRACED this slavery in debauchery and eventual demise through dissipation or dissolution as a more merciful alternative to endings through plague or hunger, leading to the spread of strange pleasure-suicide slave cults all across the cloud cities, their lives and deaths forever tainting the airy essence of these places and beings, spreading a spiritual malaise that lingers well into the Age of Sorrows, their skies now also windows into celestial spheres where the stars of beings that are not gods thread...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-07-2024, 04:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T06:52:14-08:00","id":1503805,"title":"","content":"Video game arcades exist in Creation. <br /> <br /> I don't know how I'm going to do it, but I'm somehow going to make it work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T10:43:55-08:00","id":1503825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1503805#post1503805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Video game arcades exist in Creation.<br /> <br /> I don't know how I'm going to do it, but I'm somehow going to make it work.</div> </div> </div> </div>An amusement arcade is doable but it would probably be more carnival games and the occasional clockwork automation in the style of the old coin operated machines that's probably at least boarderline irreplaceable.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T15:04:34-08:00","id":1503848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1503825#post1503825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An amusement arcade is doable but it would probably be more carnival games and the occasional clockwork automation in the style of the old coin operated machines that's probably at least boarderline irreplaceable.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what we need? Something along the lines of the Sierra Madre. A long dead gaming-arcade, with automated defenses and commerce services. Play the games, and win fabulous prizes! Or run afoul of the security's many unknown rules, and be thrown out or worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T10:18:46-08:00","id":1503903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1503805#post1503805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Video game arcades exist in Creation.<br /> <br /> I don't know how I'm going to do it, but I'm somehow going to make it work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can easily imagine two variants of this. <br /> <br /> First is an old First age amusement place which has video games and is guarded by malfunctioning automatons. <br /> <br /> Second is one that has a second circle demon themed after polybius and having First circle demons that have the typical jumanji game plays you sort of thing going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T06:24:27-08:00","id":1504198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1503903#post1503903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can easily imagine two variants of this.<br /> <br /> First is an old First age amusement place which has video games and is guarded by malfunctioning automatons.<br /> <br /> Second is one that has a second circle demon themed after polybius and having First circle demons that have the typical jumanji game plays you sort of thing going on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd definitely have technomagic arcades in the major cities, if nothing else they are powered/run by bound hegra illusion demons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T07:15:14-08:00","id":1504200,"title":"","content":"Autochthon always being paranoid of the future and the possibility that he may not be able to out heal his techno - organic cancer built a backup system into the foundations of creation, should he ever expire creation will begin an auxiliary function. Acting similar to the process of Lethe for mortals, if Autochthon were to fall to his disease his essence will be collected by creation itself and he will slowly reform from creation's features.<br /> <br /> This process was only meant for Autochthon but due to the nature of his disease he had to make the process adaptable. Then Autochthon's brothers and sisters were slain by the Exalted (normal history from this point)<br /> <br /> What Autochthon didn't know is his adaptable process for resurrecting himself has been puzzling out how to perform it's duties on the Neverborn but instead of treating them as separate entities it has been siphoning off small amounts of necrotic essence from each of them and reconstituting entirely new essence matrices.<br /> <br /> Now, in creation large amounts of essence flows through the dragon lines, pooling into multiple demesnes within close proximity to each other. Entire generations of mortals and animals alike in these areas start to have dreams and nightmares of impossible things, things they have no context for what so ever but still feel some vague connection to. Then, the last mortal or animal component comes of age and they all feel a pull. Animals, mortals, and the very landscape itself all converge between the demesnes and in just a brief moment pure chaos exists within the bounds of creation. An infinitely powerful essence singularity is formed at the heart of this bubble of pure chaos forcing causality into a bubble of chaos held within a bubble of ordered creation. For just an instance there are no laws again, time does not exist and within the chaos bubble time not has reformed. The contradiction forces the bubble to collapse on itself and a new gestalt primordial has awakened, it is both the sum of all its parts and so much more","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-11T02:26:58-08:00","id":1505095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1504198#post1504198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd definitely have technomagic arcades in the major cities, if nothing else they are powered/run by bound hegra illusion demons</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a wonderful idea. Hegra has most definitely not been used a lot. I see a lot of 1st circles for fighting, war, creation, planning, thought, but Hegra's entertainment and media and literature niche has most definitely been underused. <br /> <br /> Though Creation may vary. Some might consider those arcades to be dens where the youth are corrupted and signs of delinquency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T08:03:20-07:00","id":1505676,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I have so much headcanon I haven't shared.<br /> <br /> 1. Most crops and the vast majority of grains grown in Creation are perennial species bred in the First Age. I also have a bunch of specific ideas about cuisine, especially in Lookshy.<br /> <br /> 2. Many cultures use bronze, arsenical bronze, brass, or stone and can\u2019t smelt iron, but iron tools and weapons are still widespread, though not cheap nor common.\u200b<br /> <br /> 3. The Tarpan Wastes are not a natural desert with a failing Solar Working. There are no natural deserts on the Blessed Isle, instead it was formerly semiarid but fertile grassland. It became a series of genocidal death camps and a huge shadowland in the Usurpation, just like Marama\u2019s Fell. The Shogunate heavily salted the whole region at great expense, and returned it to Creation, but it remains too cursed for the Wood Aspects and sorcerers to restore its former fertility.\u200b<br /> <br /> 4. Linowan forge bronze and copper tools, weapons, and ornaments in addition to precious metals. They farm oaks, berries, and fruit and nut trees.\u200b<br /> <br /> 5. Halta cannot defeat or drive out the Fair Folk that took over the ground during the Balorian Crusade, and have virtually no access to iron. Faerie could easily eat them or kill their trees \u2013 ultimately, the Haltan are hostages. To not be eaten, Haltan have to keep an alliance. Sometimes Fair Folk are satisfied by theatre, staged debates, loud music, drunken revelry, worship, or the horrors of war, but many demand human sacrifice. The unacknowledged primary reason for the forever war is to sacrifice Linowans. Prisoners of war are sacrificed on the border or imported to villages farther away. Deep interior villages are rare and get by with draconian laws that make many crimes punishable by sacrifice. Linowans with some justification say all Haltan are faerie-worshipping ravagers and their whole forest is cursed.\u200b<br /> 5.5. Haltan and far-far Easterners with little access to minerals have no metallurgy or ceramic craft. They make heavy use of bone and ironwood for tools and weapons, including human bone. They use sky burials and make tools out of their relatives\u2019 bones. Haltan pave their hearths with human scapulas and skull pieces, carved to fit. They trade for the stone and metal tools necessary to carve ironwood and bone \u2013 from human trading partners and the Fair Folk. Their agriculture is easier, since they can grow various epiphytes, vines, and fungi. With no salt and minimal use of fire, most of their food is preserved by vinegar, alcohol, fermenting, or honey.\u200b<br /> <br /> 6. Lunars can create self-perpetuating beastfolk lineages based on any animal they can become, it just requires more Charm investment and effort than basing it on their spirit shape. They can absolutely breed beastfolk directly, with humans, while in human shape. Doing it in the Wyld with mismatched shapes results in Wyld mutant offspring, which pretty much nobody wants.\u200b<br /> 6.5. </span></span>\u200b<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lunars <i>can</i> breed with animals, and the results range from Moon-born but nonsapient animals, to sapient animals with some human physical traits but no human soul, to intelligent yokai-animals that can (after many years) learn to shapeshift into a human or half-human form but are definitely <i>not</i> human at all. They can never have beastfolk offspring with animals.\u200b<br /> <br /> 7. Ghosts don\u2019t make Oblivion bigger or stronger just by existing. Ancestor cults do funnel Creation\u2019s Essence into the Underworld... but ancestors who intervene in Creation funnel Essence back the other way. And Creation can\u2019t run out of Essence anyway, unless the Wyld or Underworld destroy it faster than the Poles can draw new Essence out of the infinite Wyld.\u200b<br /> <br /> 8. The preponderance of wordy, flowery names for charms and spells and the like is the result of something He Who Bleeds the Unknown Word built into the nature of Essence manipulation, back when the Primordials created the world. Whenever someone discovers a new way to channel Essence, they feel a slight compulsion to give their new ability a distinct, florid name ... even if it isn't a discrete technique.\u200b<br /> 8.5. The Dragon's Shadow undercut this by keeping all of his powers nameless, just to prove He Who Bleeds wasn't the boss of him.<br /> <br /> 9. Each Incarna has a favorite sacred animal: the mouse for Sol, the raiton for Mars, the gull for Mercury, the magpie for Jupiter, the peafowl for Venus, and the crow/raven for Saturn. Luna gives the impression of having multiple favorites, but ze actually just changes zir mind frequently.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-18-2023, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T21:21:34-07:00","id":1505754,"title":"","content":"The Tarpan I actually do as kind of a mix of canon and what you ahve. Where it was origianlly semi-arid but the Workings terraformed it. And now that they're fading, the Wastes are actually becoming desolute becuase the geomancy got so effed that now it's become more desert than it ever was to begin with.<br /> <br /> I actually did similar with the Incarna on animals, with eagles for Mars and owls for Jupiter. Tad cliche, but the other three Maidens do have bird constellations and those are ones I feel distinct enough from the other species used by them. And in Luna's cae, I actulaly had rabbits of a sort show up a lot in thier motifs due to both the East Asian stuff, and also stuff like Al-Miraj and making them kind of carnivorous mosnter-ones feels also on brand for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T18:45:35-07:00","id":1506283,"title":"","content":"It's seemingly dangerous to learn about the Yozi Cytherea, with many of the demonologists who try to find answers to this coming to sticky ends. There are four main schools of belief on this.<br /> <br /> -Cytherea cannot be known and to attempt that is to invite death and madness.<br /> -Cytherea no longer wishes to be known and will smite those who don't respect her wishes.<br /> -Cytherea has been sentenced to be a secret known only to the Yozis by her siblings who perhaps consider her a traitor.<br /> -That the fates of those who seek to learn more about Cytherea is a false correlation and that really, anyone that interested in the Yozis themselves was probably already dealing directly with the Unquestionables and generally asking for trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T12:59:37-07:00","id":1507199,"title":"","content":"By the end of the First Age, every type of individual-useable weapon known to humanity, no matter how obscure or niche, had at least one supernatural martial art built around it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T04:44:53-07:00","id":1507471,"title":"","content":"By the end of the first age, there was also a shitload of weird essence training techniques that they went around the opposite ways of martial arts. Like 'I'm so good at meditating I can punch diseases out of you'. Or 'I'm so good at taking things apart I can also put them together'. <br /> <br /> Long story short, weird bursts of semi-magical things aren't limited to martial arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T04:37:38-07:00","id":1507932,"title":"","content":"Dragonblooded of the &quot;Corpse Elements&quot; are still a thing, and tend to spring up among those born near shadowlands, or survivors of near-death experiences. They're unusually common around Linowa, and a major reason why Halta hasn't decided the war by now. There is a necromantic initiation ritual that involves burying shamanic prospects in the Field of Woe to commune with, and emerge victorious from, the spirits of the vengeful dead. <br /> <br /> Linowan necromancers seldom send the dead on raids, as the bounty of conquest is for the living, but they have called talons of dead men to the defense of their homeland, and crafted masks that allow ghostly veterans to &quot;guide&quot; young warriors directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T20:02:45-07:00","id":1507991,"title":"","content":"Some more for my stuff.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Terrestrial Inheritance Stuff</u></b><br /> I straight-up ignore the textbox on Dragon-Blooded breeding stuff in the 3e corebook. The heritablity is based on whether either parent was an Exalt first, whether that parent cultivated their Progentive Essence, and it goes down from there. It's usually not better than 50/50, but just kind of due to the vageries of statistics, and correlation and causation, a lot of &quot;strong blodlines&quot; are lucky ones that folks think have something going. It probably looks likea bell curve more than anything.<br /> <br /> Kind of additionally in this is that there's means to pass one's Progentive Essence to an adopted child. The kid still needs to be young enough, and there's still the cultivation, but there's rituals to officially adopt someone as if they're their own kid. This is the same thing that lets sorcerously-conceived children count.<br /> <br /> Kind of in this vein, some Realm prejudices might seem odd, but fitting. Someone who's actually the result of a pillow pregnancy that a guy had with the two years after his last kid might still be Will-Bred if it's bene hidden enough and the family has the prestige. Someone who's a leftover child might be considered Thin-Blooded even though thier kids are as likely to Exalt as anyone else.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Getimian Exaltation</u></b><br /> A big weirdness with Getimians is that their Exaltations were all Chosen when they were firs tcreated. Sacheverell and Oramus due to being a combination of &quot;Sees everything in the future&quot; and &quot;realizing everything possible&quot; more or less have &quot;Exalted&quot; everyone who ever will in all of history as a Getimian. This note, doens't mean they're limited. There's only the 64 and they do get inherited. It's just that it's predetermined hwen and how every single one was. And the two now-Yozi can't really stop it if they wanted to: The Exaltation is jus tpart of thier natur enow.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T13:19:33-07:00","id":1508480,"title":"","content":"I just rewatched Chernobyl, so: <br /> <br /> There's actual nuclear reactor analogues in Creation. And just as dangerous and deadly. In fact there are several famed theatres and epics based on them, from running to make sure they shut down correctly or when the evil villain (usually a Solar) tries to go into long-abandoned graveyards (read: toxic dump site) to create a deadly weapon (read: radiological terrorism), with the brave dragonblooded hero coming to stop them. Bonus points for extra drama if the brave hero dies because some of the poison got onto them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T13:34:13-07:00","id":1508482,"title":"","content":"Isn't that what Proto-Shinmatic Vortecies are? They're a niche 2e thing though, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T14:53:21-07:00","id":1508486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1508482#post1508482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that what Proto-Shinmatic Vortecies are? They're a niche 2e thing though, I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Protoshinmaic vortexes are... I believe, to be Artifact 5 things. Also, I tend to not say this but I *have* read on what they are, and frankly speaking I don't like how the artifact is written, and I don't think that from a worldbuilding standpoint they're very useful or interesting. Sure, they're nice to look at and probably good loot, but no, they don't fit. They're not... *waves hands*. They're not messy enough. <br /> <br /> I want the messiness, fear, and horror that comes with nuclear depositories. With thaumaturgy, spirits, and other stuff thrown inside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T14:59:10-07:00","id":1508487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1508486#post1508486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Protoshinmaic vortexes are... I believe, to be Artifact 5 things. Also, I tend to not say this but I *have* read on what they are, and frankly speaking I don't like how the artifact is written, and I don't think that from a worldbuilding standpoint they're very useful or interesting. Sure, they're nice to look at and probably good loot, but no, they don't fit. They're not... *waves hands*. They're not messy enough.<br /> <br /> I want the messiness, fear, and horror that comes with nuclear depositories. With thaumaturgy, spirits, and other stuff thrown inside.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Wyld-ification of the blast radius and mutations in the immediate effect isn't messy enough for you?<br /> <br /> PSVs aren't well-written overall, sure, but they fit &quot;nuclear reactor&quot; pretty well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T06:21:12-07:00","id":1508878,"title":"","content":"The most popular form of cooking in the First Age was with solar ovens partially as a gesture of piety to the Unconquered Sun but also because the carefully cultivated weather around major habitation centres made them rather practical. After the Usurpation, the Shogunate didn't have the kind of leverage with the Bureau of Seasons that their predecessors did and its increasing unreliability and natural association with ideological loyalists to the Solar Deliberative lead to its decline and in the Age of Sorrows the notion of cooking food by leaving it to bake in the sun is associated with exaggerated and fanciful tales of the south.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T05:07:18-07:00","id":1509167,"title":"","content":"In spite of the various arts a Sidereal can learn as their foundation for Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Style, Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style remains the most popular. It's esoteric enough to make practitioners start reevaluating their worldview, while still being grounded enough to be comprehensible as a bridge. Practitioners who graduated from the style view PACS through the lense of universal harmonics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T13:53:39-07:00","id":1510403,"title":"","content":"Its overstated how much the Guild consistently employs mercenaries due to some inexact terminology and situations that are more outliers than representative of standard practice as hiring mercenaries long-term tends to be ruinously expensive and doesn't ensure loyalty. A merchant prince's personal forces are most likely to be slaves or former slaves whose loyalty they feel is secured, the problem with this approach is that it doesn't scale up well or have good countermeasures for enemy Exalts.<br /> <br /> The terminology confusion is that over time families with power and influence in the Guild cultivate personal forces that over time grow in autonomy until they are essentially mercenaries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 05-01-2023, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T15:36:51-07:00","id":1514060,"title":"","content":"Maiden Tea is called such because a popular brand of oral contraceptive was effectively marketed during the First Age. Its marketing jingles still survive in some cultures to this day. <br /> <br /> (Verse 1)<br /> \u266a Are you tired of chasing storks in the sky? \u266a<br /> \u266a Want a solution that will make you sigh \u266a<br /> \u266a Introducing Maiden Tea, the answer you seek \u266a<br /> \u266a Keeps surprises at bay, every day of the week \u266a<br /> <br /> (Chorus)<br /> Maiden Tea, Maiden Tea, our secret delight \u266a No more unplanned surprises, sleep well every night \u266a Maiden Tea, Maiden Tea, your choice so wise \u266a<br /> Take control of your future, with a wink and a sigh \u266a<br /> <br /> (Verse 2)<br /> \u266a Say goodbye to baby booms and nursery rhymes \u266a<br /> \u266a Maiden Tea keeps you dancing, no worries, no chimes \u266a<br /> \u266a Just one cup a day, and you're ready to go \u266a<br /> \u266a Take charge of your life, let your confidence grow \u266a<br /> <br /> (Chorus)<br /> \u266a Maiden Tea, Maiden Tea, our secret delight \u266a<br /> \u266a No more unplanned surprises, sleep well every night \u266a<br /> \u266a Maiden Tea, Maiden Tea, your choice so wise \u266a<br /> \u266a Take control of your future, with a wink and a sigh \u266a<br /> <br /> (Bridge)<br /> \u266a Laughter and freedom, that's what it brings \u266a<br /> \u266a With Maiden Tea, embrace life's exciting things \u266a<br /> \u266a No more worrying 'bout the stork at your door \u266a<br /> \u266a Maiden Tea keeps surprises away, forevermore \u266a<br /> <br /> (Chorus)<br /> \u266a Maiden Tea, Maiden Tea, our secret delight \u266a<br /> \u266a No more unplanned surprises, sleep well every night \u266a<br /> \u266a Maiden Tea, Maiden Tea, your choice so wise \u266a<br /> \u266a Take control of your future, with a wink and a sigh \u266a<br /> <br /> (Outro)<br /> \u266a So, ladies, embrace your power and seize the day \u266a<br /> \u266a With Maiden Tea, you're in control all the way \u266a<br /> \u266a Enjoy life's adventures, worry-free and bold \u266a<br /> \u266a Maiden Tea, your secret weapon, never gets old \u266a\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T00:48:54-07:00","id":1514282,"title":"","content":"Lytek sounds and acts like Nigel Thornberry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T07:17:09-07:00","id":1514467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1514282#post1514282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lytek sounds and acts like Nigel Thornberry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Marvelous!<br /> <br /> There are funeral cults for the Primordials that became Neverborn hidden across Creation, praying in order to sooth the souls of these fallen Creators. Initially this was set up by a secret faction of the Solar Deliberative in order to minimize the activity of said Neverborn within Creation (much like how the Dragonblooded gave Solars great tombs after the Usurpation to prevent ghosts). How effective this is remains unknown though it should be noted that membership activity has been at it's lowest around the Contagion and right before the Emperess disappeared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T16:50:01-07:00","id":1515585,"title":"","content":"1: If a Solar and a Lunar exaltation are bonded and both free (i.e one isn't bound up in a currently living Exalt) they almost invariably exalt their mates at the same age at the same time.<br /> <br /> Why? Because I came up with a fun little concept of two like 11-year-old kids exalting as a Twilight and a Changing Moon--which I must stress is portrayed as two adorable kids with puppy crushes on each other--and it's a cute idea, I dunno.<br /> <br /> 2: On a completely unrelated note (/srs), Getimians are basically Everything Everywhere All At Once jumpers, in that they can access the abilities of alternate universe versions of themselves. Mechanically, I'd represent this as them being able to that Infected Fate power they have from Essence on <i>themselves</i>--they tie their own personal destiny with some AU version of themselves (and if I'm feeling spicy, they can do it to <i>other</i> people, meaning they can suddenly make that Dragon-Blood they're fighting do a dance-off because in some Modern shard timeline they became a DDR pro) Do they also have to do some bizarre and nonsensical thing to trigger it like EEAAO jumpers? ...that's for you to decide. And yeah, I do kinda want high-essence Getimians to basically just be Jobu Tupaki. Sue me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","user":"Frostav","date":". 06-19-2023, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T03:14:55-07:00","id":1515997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1515585#post1515585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2: On a completely unrelated note (/srs), Getimians are basically Everything Everywhere All At Once jumpers, in that they can access the abilities of alternate universe versions of themselves. Mechanically, I'd represent this as them being able to that Infected Fate power they have from Essence on <i>themselves</i>--they tie their own personal destiny with some AU version of themselves (and if I'm feeling spicy, they can do it to <i>other</i> people, meaning they can suddenly make that Dragon-Blood they're fighting do a dance-off because in some Modern shard timeline they became a DDR pro) Do they also have to do some bizarre and nonsensical thing to trigger it like EEAAO jumpers? ...that's for you to decide. And yeah, I do kinda want high-essence Getimians to basically just be Jobu Tupaki. Sue me.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me that's more how I'd define the Nocturnals fansplat. Getimians seem like they'd have a very clear idea of who they were in their Origin and be inclined to bring Creation more into line with it. To me it's the difference between Evelyn Wang and Philippa Georgiou aka Her Most Imperial Majesty, Mother of the Fatherland, Overlord of Vulcan, Dominus of Qo'noS, Regina Andor, Philippa Georgiou Augustus Iaponius Centarius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T05:21:37-07:00","id":1516092,"title":"","content":"There's at least one Beastfolk kingdom in the East that resembles the Lizardman lands from Warhammer Fantasy. 3+ distinct lineages descended from a variety of reptilian Lunars, each lineage originating from -and perpetuated by, in emergencies- a set of &quot;spawning pool&quot; <u>Beast-Soul Awakening Crucible</u>s. The toad-folk rule, and are often Thaumaturges or Sorcerers. The River Dragon-folk are laborers and muscle. Gecko-folk are scouts and scribes. Etc.<br /> <br /> Not the most original headcannon, I know. But I also like to think this kingdom is continually re-inherited by the same Lunar Exaltation, who is expected to build an additional Crucible with every incarnation. Which becomes interesting, when the latest incarnation's Spirit Shape is NOT reptilian.<br /> <br /> Edit: come to think of it, Skaven might make good minions for Smiling Rat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 06-25-2023, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T18:25:21-07:00","id":1516574,"title":"","content":"The Emissary of Nexus is a cabal of several powerful Exigents linked with an Artifact N/A costume.<br /> The Emissary's Regalia allows multiple users to attune to it, and allows all attuned users to be aware of the circumstances around the current wearer, as well as telepathic communication between attuned users.<br /> Those attuned can spend motes to instantly swap places, one switching into the Regalia and the other teleporting away. Regardless of which user is wearing it, the cost of the Regalia's Evocations can be paid by any attuned user.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T23:09:10-07:00","id":1517628,"title":"","content":"The Viator of Nullspace is a combination of Divine Minister and demon. Autochthon internalized his siblings' constant abuse until he subconsciously adopted their hate of him and the pain they inflicted on him as his own. The Dread Gear personifies his trauma, his belief that he deserves to be under constant attack (because why else would his siblings have kept doing it?), and the inscrutable sense of wrongness he feels when he goes for too long without being attacked. The other Divine Ministers don't talk about the Viator's origins for fear that reliving the memories will trigger a flashback in Autochthon that summons the Viator again: the only defense they can think of is to repress the Viator and hope nothing prompts the Great Maker's CPTSD for the rest of eternity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 07-10-2023, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T04:33:41-07:00","id":1518021,"title":"","content":"Ah. In other words... Autochthon needs therapy. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, he can go back to creation and start unleashing all that fury on Malfeas. Beating up the quivering, helpless bodies of your tormentors should be cathartic, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T04:57:31-07:00","id":1518023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1518021#post1518021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, he can go back to creation and start unleashing all that fury on Malfeas. Beating up the quivering, helpless bodies of your tormentors should be cathartic, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Engine of Extinction has entered the chat, I see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T16:09:07-07:00","id":1519204,"title":"","content":"You know, I'm not sure if this is needed but I&quot;m going to say this: There are more mortal sorcerers in Creation than Dragonblooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 07-30-2023, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T18:46:42-07:00","id":1519539,"title":"","content":"So this falls under the heading of &quot;I'd never state this at the table, but in my own head...&quot;<br /> <br /> Most of the world knows the Scarlet Empress' name. Many even use it. It's never used at the table, however, as &quot;The Scarlet Empress&quot; is her Posthumous Name and it's effectively dubbed/edited in by the players whenever her name would be spoken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T18:54:36-07:00","id":1519540,"title":"","content":"Really? I'm more fond of the idea that her name is lost to time - a combination of Immaculate propaganda enshrining her as <b>THE</b> Empress, and her own machinations in the early days to overcome being a no-name Shogunate Lieutenant (I think that was the rank she was mentioned as holding? It was a low-rank officer, at any rate). <br /> <br /> Or that her old name now just means &quot;Scarlet Empress&quot;, due to linguistic drift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T08:43:09-07:00","id":1519746,"title":"","content":"People really overthink the name thing, when there have been innumerable real life monarchs who adopt new names, many of which are pretty much just titles, on assuming the throne.<br /> <br /> Until anything says that the syllables composing the personal name of the Scarlet Empress became forbidden to write in any context, her approach to the issue is actually fairly tame compared to some examples from China.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T13:52:32-08:00","id":1525480,"title":"","content":"Abyssal Exalted who have been at it for a while have a tendency to drift away from &quot;living&quot; being a natural part of their vocabulary for how to categorise people. After enough time, they start to think of people in terms of the categories of &quot;dead&quot; and &quot;not yet dead&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T00:57:55-08:00","id":1525678,"title":"","content":"I talked about language stuff before, but here's some more in-depth thoughts on how I have chopped-up and describe the different language families of Creation that I use for my games. I use a modified Languages Merit also in my house rules document.<br /> <br /> <b>Language Families Revisited</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The core rulebook is often inconsistent about whether a given language is a language or a language family. The list below revised a few of the less clear groups to better fit the idea of being a language family, or a language with many mutually intelligible dialects as listed below. Note that while some languages do have major families, not all languages fall into those families. For example, while Windspeak and Winterspeak are the largest subfamilies of Skytongue, the Yasari language spoken amongst the people of Jazrafel, Jazmir, and its neighboring peninsula does not fall into either family. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>High Realm</b> was originally the language of the W\u00e0n people of the Northeastern Blessed Isle. While the version spoken throughout the Realm for administrative purposes and by the ruling class is by far the most prominent version, with dialects representing regional variants found in the home cities of different Great Houses, cadet houses like those of Cherak, the Dragon Caste of Prasad, Port Calin, and the ruling class of Zhaojun. The W\u00e0n </span> language is related to <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">many of the native languages of residents of the Dragon\u2019s Blanket and Imperial River Basin areas, including Pangu and the Imperial City itself. Dragon Tongue is considered a particularly esoteric dialect of Dynastic High Realm. It is also in some areas spoken as the native tongue in cities like Juche and Mnemon-Darjilis, where the local languages have been actively repressed by the ruling Great House. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Low Realm</b> represents the numerous local languages of other areas of the Blessed Isle from before the rise of the Scarlet Empress, with Arjuf especially notable by still using its own language for many local uses even amongst its higher classes. Languages include Arjufi, Myionese, and the languages of other pre-Dynasty polities throughout the Isle and some of the Southern Threshold North of An-Teng. A notable subfamily of languages is Mountainspeak, which includes the langauge found in Lord\u2019s Crossing and the suppressed language of Juche. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Skytongue</b> has two main subfamilies: <b>Windspeak</b> and <b>Winterspeak</b>. The former is concentrated primarily on the Peninsular North, with Medo being the Southernmost area to speak a language, while the area East of Malice bay serves as a transition area to more languages of Foresttongue. The latter is spoken primarily along the coast of the White Sea, parts of Malice Bay, and much of Mela\u2019s Fangs. Many of the more isolated communities in the Direction speak a multitude of language isolates, some barely intelligible to speakers of the main branches of Skytongue. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Riverspeak</b> is a unique language family, which due to the position of the River Province over hte centuries contains many languages that contain vocabulary and grammar from Windspeak, Foresttongue, and Summerspeak. The language most-used through much of Creation\u2019s trade networks is based on the administrative language of old Hollow, and standardized by the Academy of Language found in Nexus. This institution publishes an updated grammar and dictionary manual that are often considered the standard for international trade, with mass woodblock printed versions distributed throughout the Threshold every seventeen years. This prescriptive version of Riverspeak does not often capture many of the nuances or variants found throughout the River Province. It barely resembles how most people speak in Nexus day-to-day, Lookshyan official records continue to use a language and script popular with the Eastern Shogunate that is otherwise dead, Port Calin still maintains a sizable population of High Realm speakers, and Greyfalls has notable elements of both High Realm and Forestongue in the speech of its locals.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Foresttongue</b> is the most widely distributed language families and thus the most diverse, with languages found amongst those conquered by the Empire of the Bear in the North, while the people of Volivat speak a barely-recognizable language in the Dreaming Sea. The most widely spoken languages are those used by the rulers of Mahalanka and Ixoatli, which use the language in both administrative and day to day life, as well as through trade. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Flametongue</b> has two major subfamilies: <b>Ashtongue</b> and <b>Summertongue</b>. Ashtongue along with Seatongue encompasses many languages found throughout the lands West of the Firepeak Mountains, and populations on the Eastern side from Dajaz all the way to Paragon. It is also notably the language family which many of the Delzahn languages fall within. Summertongue meanwhile encompasses many of the languages of the Varang City States, the native languages of Chiaroscuro, and along with Forestongue many of the languages along the Dreaming Sea. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Due to the myriad of islands and accompanying communites in the West<b>, Seatongue</b> is often one of the hardest families to navigate, with many islands having their own unique languages or dialects, sometimes more than one. Trade is generally conducted using the language of one of the major powers when possible, with the language of Abalone becoming the de facto trade language of Realm satrapies over the last few decades, although knowledge of Onyxian has become more prominent in recent years. Seatongue is also found in the Southwest, intermingling with Ashtongue in a quilted patchwork of languages, as well as along the coasts of the Northwest, with the creole of Coral Seatongue found in use in Fajadi ports, as well as a few terms which have made their way into the local speech of Bittern and Uluiru. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Tribal Tongues</span></b> also represent language isolates which can be found on every corner of Creation, from the Isle of Graces in the Northwest to the Old Realm-derived langauge of the sorcerers of Ysyr. Some exist even on the Blessed Isle, where some of the pre-W\u00e0n languages continue to be spoken in everyday life, although languages like the native speech of Darjilis or the Tarpan Wastes are close to extinction due to efforts of ruling Great Houses or simple lack of econimc opportunties in its use. The various unique ancient languages spoken among the mortal and Dragon-Blooded families of the Heaven's Dragons would also be considered such languages.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Old Realm</span></b> predates the native language of any mortal being and is also not a langauge of any mortal being. Language can change quickly and it had long stopped being the main language of humanity since the Time Before, and any attempt for communities to use it exclusively oftne results in a strange language isolate that is no more able to communicate with supernatural beings as it can any other human group. It also has had deliberately crafted versions which were utilized by humans for specific contexts, such as the syllabary ideograms of Second Deliberative's official annals, the flowing abjad of the original manuscript of <i>The White Treatise</i>, the alien script of Rathess' Holy High Speech, or the dense and complex ideographic and tonal langauge used to encode spells within the <i>Book of Three Circles</i>. Other dialects of Old Realm include those natively spoken by supernatural beings like the Fair Folk, various species of demons, the elemental races, or the strange singular tongues of behemoths. Beings who speak Old Realm natively always understand all other dialects. A character must have the Weird Tongue Merit in order to speak Old Realm.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Autochthonian</b> languages descend from the ancient m\u00e9lange of tongues spoken by the original exiles to the Realm of Brass and Shadow, many members of entire families extinct in Creation today. Each Nation of the Octet has its own official language, though communities within a Nation will often have their own distinct dialects, while years of cultural admixture between Nations has also resulted in a large body of shared vocabulary and grammar between them. They all generally use the same writing system, which is derived from a simplified form of Old Realm glyphs, often with developed idiographic meaning to help facilitate international communication. Additionally, a notable portion of Autocthhonian population is versed in the use of hand and other bodily gestures that allow communication in environments where equipment or loud noise would make speech otherwise impossible, as well as facilitating residents who normally cannot hear either nor speak inherently or due to injury in the indsutrail environment of the Great Maker. While such \u201cHand Talk\u201d languages vary between and within Nations, it often is the first means of communication between unidentified groups and considered a standard element of Autocthonian speech spoken natively along more widely recognized forms of language. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 03-04-2024, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T07:40:01-08:00","id":1525907,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if it counts as headcanon, but in the camapign I'm building, the Silver Pact's vendetta against the Realm is only partly genuine. After the Contagion and the Fair Folk invasion they founded a ring of dominions 1st Age ruins at the edge of the Wyld and in forsaken Shadowlands, to fortify Creation against external threats, while staying out of Heavens sight. They use their war against the Realm both to keep it busy and contained so it won't disrupt their operations, and as a way to get whatever resources they can't find in those dominions in order to get them back in fighting shape by 1st Age standards. They also use those dominions to funnel mystical resources, moonsilver, fae magics and such, back into Creation's dominions to help the War effort against the Realm.<br /> While Heaven and the Bronze faction can't truly watch those liminal dominions, they're aware of their existence and purpose and find them useful enough that they don't push for a decisive strike against Lunar guerilla in Creation, in spite of knowing the Silver Pact is stretched thin. And also because they don't know what 1st Age WMD the pact might have recovered out there.<br /> The return of the Solars, the rise of the Abyssals and the advent of the Infernals is threatening to tip that balance as Solars reclaim territory from the Realm and the Wyld, Abyssals carve their own kingdoms in the Underworld and Shadowlands, while Infernals are destabilizing both Satrapies and Lunar dominions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T17:16:59-08:00","id":1526196,"title":"","content":"Gaia agreed to kill her family because her girlfriend asked her to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T17:38:18-08:00","id":1526197,"title":"","content":"Now that just <i>is</i> cannon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T19:19:57-08:00","id":1526262,"title":"","content":"Soulsteel caste Alchemicals were prototypes for Nebiru's Chosen, which ultimately did play out with the Umbrals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T23:06:18-08:00","id":1526266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1526262#post1526262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soulsteel caste Alchemicals were prototypes for Nebiru's Chosen, which ultimately did play out with the Umbrals.</div> </div> </div> </div>This honestly I think is the actual case with Soulsteel and Adamants to Umbrals and Aurorals respectively. The optional bit is whether Umbrals or Hearteaters are actually a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T00:40:29-08:00","id":1530616,"title":"","content":"Mine is - The Great Curse does not affect the Exaltations it affects the world. It made the world a place where human nature could never live up to the responsibility of such tremendous power. The cycles of debauchery, rebellion, overthrow, and slow decline into a new decadence are all symptoms of the same curse. Even without Exalted Creation would still have the Curse eating at the heart of everyone with any form of power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I used to be Median but life has made me Mean.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1753-avrjoe","name":"Avrjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1753_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-17T11:09:29-08:00","id":1531028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avrjoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1530616#post1530616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mine is - The Great Curse does not affect the Exaltations it affects the world. It made the world a place where human nature could never live up to the responsibility of such tremendous power. The cycles of debauchery, rebellion, overthrow, and slow decline into a new decadence are all symptoms of the same curse. Even without Exalted Creation would still have the Curse eating at the heart of everyone with any form of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>ooh, I like this one. Its not 'how do you affect the unaffectable'? They don't. They just permanently lessen Creation spiritually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T19:05:28-08:00","id":1531488,"title":"","content":"What are the Lintha really, dilluted inheritors of a pre-human legacy like Jadeborn or Dragon Kings, persevering descendants of a lineage of demon-blooded favored by Kimbery since the Time Before, a cesspool of multiple legacies with dreams of grandeur and the pedigree of polluted water?<br /> <br /> <i><b>Yes</b></i><br /> <br /> The Lintha of the Time of Tumult are unlike the Lintha from before Dukantha, who are unlike the Lintha from before Contagion, who are unlike the Lintha of the First Age and who might be looked askance upon by their alien forebears - delve deep enough into their mausoleums of salt &amp; brine preserved carcasses enfolded in seaweed wrappings and one may find finery and forms ever more alien, some like pelagothropes or beastfolk, others with markings of the blood of dragons or elementals, beings with an almost idealized cast closer to the greatest of Jadeborn than any man or woman born from a human womb, but also older and stranger beings, between reptilian or piscine, more akin to homage or mockeries of Mosok &amp; their brethren and older more eldritch besides.<br /> <br /> Because the Lintha are the beloved of the Sea that Went Against the Flame, they ebb and flow, they corrode and mix up with whatever crosses their path, in an endless cycle of acretion and infusion, condemned to tides of repetitive transformation that yet produces utterly different beings.<br /> <br /> The ghosts of the Lintha are more aware of these layers of difference as the ancestors of certain epochs serve as mediators between themselves and layers of older ancestors deeper in the Sea of Shadows than them, who themselves will sometimes comment or hint of even more ancient and alien beings on greater depths that communicate in ways no human-like throat could even vocalize, above or below water, though only a very few of them moved to Bluehaven with the other, &quot;younger&quot; ancestors, their time already past in an era when Ng Ooro was a great land that might as well be a continent.<br /> <br /> But the seas one constant is the tides of change. That which flows may ebb, low tide gives way to high tide. That which is buried may be uncovered when the currents are right. Who's to say what form, old or new, will the Lintha take as the tides of war churn Creation asunder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-10-2024, 07:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T11:55:37-08:00","id":1531968,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that gods have nicknames for Sidereals that occasionally show up in obscure books on incidents. However, Sidereals being a self-keeping secret by reality this just means occasionally there's references to a god describing an incident as resolved due to stuff like, &quot;The fool interrupted the spider's work.&quot; that get written off as weird esoteric language/.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T09:08:16-08:00","id":1532087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1531968#post1531968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea that gods have nicknames for Sidereals that occasionally show up in obscure books on incidents. However, Sidereals being a self-keeping secret by reality this just means occasionally there's references to a god describing an incident as resolved due to stuff like, &quot;The fool interrupted the spider's work.&quot; that get written off as weird esoteric language/.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding to this, there's an entire part of Creation's mythology and pop culture involving people taking the words of spirits, gods, and exalts as being far more ominous or 'deep' than it really is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T01:51:05-08:00","id":1532142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1531968#post1531968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea that gods have nicknames for Sidereals that occasionally show up in obscure books on incidents. However, Sidereals being a self-keeping secret by reality this just means occasionally there's references to a god describing an incident as resolved due to stuff like, &quot;The fool interrupted the spider's work.&quot; that get written off as weird esoteric language/.</div> </div> </div> </div>Little aside, you just reminded me of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1459009#post1459009\">this</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T17:45:19-07:00","id":1542808,"title":"","content":"All demons are ultra specialised with one exception. That is, all demons have a particular shtick that makes them incredibly dangerous, easily surpassing any mortal at its baseline without considering charms. A blood ape will always defeat you in hand to hand combat. A sesseljae had already surpassed what's possible for any mortal doctor. Their other skills? Not so much. <br /> <br /> Which is why in Creation one of the ways to deal with them is forcing them into a contest where they aren't specialised in. They tend to be terrible at this, sometimes losing even to untalented mortals.<br /> <br /> With one exception. All demons have at least 6 dice for performance, whether it is skill in drums, singing, or dance. It is one of the few joys they never regret.<br /> <br /> And one more: <br /> <br /> Just as there are gods who became obsolete because of technology changes, there are also demons who became nearly useless after the collapse in technology from the ages of strife. Such as a near extinct species of anuhle meant to interface with the crystalline thinking crystal slabs of the solar league.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T00:32:16-07:00","id":1542857,"title":"","content":"There's an entire small 'conspiracy' of gods that are reaching down from heaven into Creation, contacting sorcerers, thaumaturges, and god-blooded. What are they doing? What's their plan? <br /> <br /> What are they trying to do?<br /> <br /> Well, its all relatively benign. In the Balorian Crusade and the Great Contagion, many gods lost their jobs as their portfolios were wrecked. The god of artificial flight got off easy, since at least someone knows about balloons. But some gods weren't okay. Their entire nations were destroyed, the species they were in charge of were rendered extinct, or the cultural activity they presided over disappeared with the culture as they fell beneath the twin catalysms. <br /> <br /> And so these gods try to regain their status and their power, or at least some of them by trying to revive, or replace, what they had lost. Thaumaturges use selective breeding and spells to try and convert wastelands back into the verdant forests and fields they once were. Sorcerers are paid in Ambrosia and Quintessence to create entire new species or restore long destroyed records. God-blooded are hired as champions and promoters of various causes to one nifty festival to a particular tasty treat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T22:05:49-07:00","id":1543137,"title":"","content":"Once upon a time between plagues and wars, a person lost its arm. No one alive knows its name, face or gender anymore, only that in a place of magic that will change with the telling, that person found the secrets ways of sorcery and adopted a claw of the wood dragon in its stead. Arm, sorcerous blessing and artifact weapon all in one, the sorcerer or sorceress would delve deeply in its essence, producing many wonders and miracles through evocations drawn from its whorls &amp; grains. So much so that when one day that magician died, the Claw would live on as an artifact on its own, a heirloom and phylactery of sorts, preserving a shade of that sorcerer as a spirit of sorts within its slumbering branches.<br /> <br /> Its fate is the source of countless, sometimes contradicting tales.<br /> <br /> In one, that Wood Dragon Claw would become the royal relic of a city-state or country the sorcerer founded, guiding - or possessing - its successors across the generations.<br /> <br /> According to others, each man or woman to succeed the founder would also learn to master the original spell - and with each ruler's passing, another living Wood Dragon Claw would come to be in the kingdom, until the palace's garden was surrounded by sorcerous shrubs that await the fateful time to awaken and be wielded once again by champions.<br /> <br /> On another, the sorcerous artifact would denude itself of all its leaves, that would spread into the four winds in the form of parchments telling of its story and the mysteries of its unique path into a sort of immortality or godhood perhaps. Texts that would spring to life a hundred heretic societies across the Dreaming Sea and beyond.<br /> <br /> And then there are those that speak of that arm-sized branch turning into a full tree, a sapling that would grow mighty in worship of its legend through generations and centuries into Moloch, a giant of ironwood, a dormant colossus that will turn into a living, breathing, moving xoanon, a warstrider of jade-hard wood of motives as mysterious as the nature that leads it to take people as riders or offerings from time to time.<br /> <br /> Which of these tales are true, if any of them, is hard to say unless one meets any of those esoteric things - and then there are those rare, bold if not mad few that would dare say all of them are, in some form or another. But if so, who can say for sure what purpose would serve such a garden of Wood Dragon Claws and the even stranger ascended colossus of lumber that indirectly cultivated all of them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-23T01:34:57-08:00","id":1547905,"title":"","content":"Artifact equipment tend to have an affinity for where they end up when an Elsewhere charm is used. (Assuming the charm doesn't designate some sort of location.) This doesn't violate the issue of charms sending things elsewhere being safe and in unimportant areas, just that some artifacts tend to end up in appropriate areas for them. Some elemental court or homes recognize artifacts appearing there as akin to a guest arriving unannounced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-24T00:19:37-08:00","id":1547924,"title":"","content":"Kind of not stated, but due to implications that machine spirits show up when you call them with the demon summoning spells in 3e, Gaian spirits can be beckoned that way too. It's just that like machine spirits, they are only able to be called, not bound. And also unlike machine spirits, <i>don't</i> like when someone calls them up without a damned good reason, regardless of their Exalt type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-24T05:46:30-08:00","id":1547929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1442105-your-headcanon-ii?p=1443089#post1443089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted is not the prehistory of wither the WoD or the CoD.<br /> <br /> It is in fact a future of the WoD. I base this on how the description of the canon ending in <i>Ascension</i> resembles the Deep Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>This made it into my new headcannon modifying some of my old headcannon<br /> <br /> everything is cyclical, creation leads to a flavor of OWoD or CWoD and then back to creation. This cycle allows for the birth of new Primordials through the potential of the Infernal Exalted. Lethe was not meant for Primordials but Auto and Gaia snuck a backdoor reincarnation mechanism into creation that funnels a dead or dieing Primordial's essence into creation and eventually into a small piece of landscape and an assortment of unexalted sentient and non sentient beings that all begin converging on the landscape. Once enough are there a new demesne is created that eventually could awaken as a new Primordial being","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}